; partypage.eval - a party built on the CREATION PAGE starts the game it shows
; (docs/party-creation-plan.md, phase 3).
;
; Run ON ITS OWN, first thing:  Dungeon.exe -headless -eval <this file>
; The page lives on the title screen, and `partypage open` refuses anywhere
; else - so this cannot follow a suite that has already started a game.
;
; Every line is one of the page's own edits (the methods its widgets call), so
; this is the page's code path, not a second one. What it should show:
;   - the page opens on one new member, refusing to start ("needs a name");
;   - Kira, an elf: STR 9 DEX 14 VIT 8 WIL 10 INT 11 after DEX +2 (the elf's
;     DEX +2 INT +1 / VIT -2 STR -1 on 10), Blades and Throwing at level 2, a
;     dagger in hand and a rock in the pack;
;   - Default party replaces her with the four; Brand turned orc becomes a made
;     member (STR 13 VIT 11 INT 8 WIL 8) with no kit; two removed;
;   - Start: `roster` prints exactly the three the page last showed, and the
;     game is playing.

logecho on
state
partypage open
partypage

partypage set name=Kira race=elf portrait=portrait135
partypage spend dex 2
partypage skill 0 blade
partypage skill 1 throwing
partypage item 0 dagger
partypage item 1 rock
partypage

partypage default
partypage set race=orc
partypage select 3
partypage set name=Old_Tilo
partypage remove 1
partypage remove 1
partypage add
partypage set name=Kira race=elf portrait=portrait135
partypage spend dex 2
partypage skill 0 blade
partypage item 0 dagger
partypage

partypage start
roster
state
